{"answerArea":{"calculator":false,"chi2Table":false,"periodicTable":false,"tTable":false,"zTable":false},"hints":[{"content":"To factor means to rewrite an expression as a product. Let's try dividing the expression $20r+60t$ by each factor.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"####Factoring out $4$\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}20r+60t\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=4\\left(\\dfrac{20r+60t}{4}\\right)\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=4\\left(\\dfrac{20r}{4}+\\dfrac{60t}{4}\\right) \\\\\\\\\n\u0026=4(5r+15t)\n\\end{align}$\n\nYes, $20r+60t$ is equivalent to $4(5r+15t)$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"####Factoring out $5$\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}20r+60t\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=5\\left(\\dfrac{20r+60t}{5}\\right)\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=5\\left(\\dfrac{20r}{5}+\\dfrac{60t}{5}\\right) \\\\\\\\\n\u0026=5(4r+12t)\n\\end{align}$\n\nNo, $20r+60t$ is *not* equivalent to $5(5r+12)$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"####Factoring out $60$\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}20r+60t\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=60\\left(\\dfrac{20r+60t}{60}\\right)\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=60\\left(\\dfrac{20r}{60}+\\dfrac{60t}{60}\\right) \\\\\\\\\n\u0026=60\\left(\\dfrac{1}{3}r+t\\right)\n\\end{align}$\n\nNo, $20r+60t$ is *not* equivalent to $60(20r+t)$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"####Factoring out $20$\n\n$\\begin{align}\n\u0026\\phantom{=}20r+60t\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=20\\left(\\dfrac{20r+60t}{20}\\right)\\\\\\\\\n\u0026=20\\left(\\dfrac{20r}{20}+\\dfrac{60t}{20}\\right) \\\\\\\\\n\u0026=20(r+3t)\n\\end{align}$\n\nYes, $20r+60t$ is equivalent to $20(r+3t)$.","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}},{"content":"The following expressions are equivalent to $20r+60t$:\n\n- $4(5r+15t)$\n- $20(r+3t)$","images":{},"replace":false,"widgets":{}}],"itemDataVersion":{"major":0,"minor":1},"question":{"content":"**Factor $20r+60t$ to identify the equivalent expressions.**\n\n[[☃ radio 1]]","images":{},"widgets":{"radio 1":{"alignment":"default","graded":true,"options":{"choices":[{"clue":"This expression is equivalent to $20r+60t$.","content":"$4(5r+15t)$","correct":true},{"clue":"This expression is equivalent to $25r+60$.","content":"$5(5r+12)$","correct":false},{"clue":"This expression is equivalent to $1200r+60t$.","content":"$60(20r+t)$","correct":false,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false},{"clue":"This expression is equivalent to $20r+60t$.","content":"$20(r+3t)$","correct":true,"isNoneOfTheAbove":false}],"countChoices":true,"deselectEnabled":false,"displayCount":null,"hasNoneOfTheAbove":false,"multipleSelect":true,"randomize":false},"static":false,"type":"radio","version":{"major":1,"minor":0}}}}}
